ow when something's  wrong you have to do something I find  this film energizing and I think one of  the things I like about it is is it  feels righteous and empowering in a way  that does not necessarily demand a  violent response because while V himself  has made the decision to employ violence  and explosions to make its point I think  ultimately the note that it ends on is  much more if we make them hear us then  we are mighty not necessarily blow that  up I may be and maybe that's me trying  to square a circle so that I don't have  to cop to a film I really like possibly  being read as an endorsement of violent  action but I do think enough about the  presentation  and showing the value of all the all the  people who aren't V and what they do  does a lot to keep that in line and keep  that in check because you know the  people who march don't slaughter the the  police presence  they just keep marching v relies on  violence but the other people don't have  to and it's them we end with so I I feel  that that helps balance what otherwise  could have been a very problematic  message maybe other people still find it  problematic and I'm not necessarily sure  I can argue against that but there you  go V for Vendetta I still haven't read  the graphic novel I should but I do  really love this movie I think it looks  great I think it's paced great I think  the acting is phenomenal I love the heck  out of this have you rewatched it lately  whatever your thoughts are drop  something down in the comments let's  talk about it bunch of stuff to do as  well buttons links merch subscribe  patreon it's all down there click on  stuff it'll take you places or don't I'm  not running a fascist government I'm not  gonna tell you what you have to do you  make your own decisions because you are  the Council  I'm just running the meetings and until  next time this council is adjourned  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

